<http://data.silknow.org/event/ca7d38a5-4cc1-36aa-b376-50c7586fd629>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This bookcase, in the Greek style, was made for the library of Carlton House, London, the home of the Prince of Wales, later the Prince Regent. The furniture was supplied by the firm of William Marsh and Thomas Tatham, possibly to designs by Charles HeathcoteTatham, William's brother, who published an influential book of Classical designs in 1799."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0a420462-dcb0-399b-a0a6-c62e78845b08> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This bookcase, in the Greek style, was made for the library of Carlton House, London, the home of the Prince of Wales, later the Prince Regent. The furniture was supplied by the firm of William Marsh and Thomas Tatham, possibly to designs by Charles HeathcoteTatham, William's brother, who published an influential book of Classical designs in 1799."@en .

